{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0022403","isObsolete":false,"name":"cell cycle phase","definition":{"text":"One of the distinct periods or stages into which the cell cycle is divided. Each phase is characterized by the occurrence of specific biochemical and morphological events."},"comment":"Note that this term should not be used for direct annotation. If you are trying to make an annotation to x phase, it is likely that the correct annotation is 'regulation of x/y phase transition' or to a process which occurs during the reported phase (i.e mitotic DNA replication for mitotic S-phase). To capture the phase when a specific location or process is observed, the phase term can be used in an annotation extension (PMID:24885854) applied to a cellular component term (with the relation exists_during) or a biological process term (with the relation happens_during).","children":[{"id":"GO:0051322","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0000279","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0051320","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0051318","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0044838","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0051319","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0051325","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0051326","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0098763","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0098762","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0051324","relation":"is_a"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2014-07-18","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044848 (biological phase)"},{"timestamp":"2014-07-18","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0022402 (cell cycle process)"},{"timestamp":"2013-05-03","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"One of the distinct periods or stages into which the cell cycle is divided. Each phase is characterized by the occurrence of specific biochemical and morphological events."},{"timestamp":"2013-05-03","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A cell cycle process comprising the steps by which a cell progresses through one of the biochemical and morphological phases and events that occur during successive cell replication or nuclear replication events."},{"timestamp":"2013-04-19","action":"Added","category":"SUBSET","text":"gocheck_do_not_annotate"},{"timestamp":"2008-05-13","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A cell cycle process comprising the steps by which a cell progresses through one of the biochemical and morphological phases and events that occur during successive cell replication or nuclear replication events."},{"timestamp":"2008-05-12","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A cell cycle process comprising the steps by which a cell progresses through one of the biochemical and morphological phases and events that occur during successive cell replication or nuclear replication events."},{"timestamp":"2008-04-01","action":"Updated","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0022402 (cell cycle process)"},{"timestamp":"2007-04-20","action":"Updated","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A cell cycle process comprising the steps by which a cell progresses through one of the biochemical and morphological phases and events that occur during successive cell replication or nuclear replication events."},{"timestamp":"2007-01-15","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A cell cycle process composed of one of the morphological steps through which a cell progresses during successive cell replication or nuclear replication events."},{"timestamp":"2007-01-15","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"cell cycle phase"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"None"}],"pageInfo":null}